      "title": "Testnet vs Mainnet: What is the Difference?",
      "excerpt": "Understand the difference between zero-risk testnet airdrops and high-reward mainnet interactions.",
      "content": "In blockchain development, a Testnet is an experimental environment where developers and users can test applications without using real money. Tokens on a testnet have zero financial value. Testnet airdrops are great for beginners because they require no capital.\n\nMainnet, on the other hand, is the live, production version of the blockchain. Transactions here require real crypto to pay for gas fees. Because users risk real capital, mainnet airdrops historically pay out significantly higher rewards than testnets.\n\nA balanced airdrop strategy involves farming highly anticipated mainnets while consistently interacting with new testnets for risk-free exposure."
