      "excerpt": "Crucial security tips to ensure you never lose your crypto while hunting for airdrops.",
      "content": "The airdrop space is unfortunately filled with bad actors trying to steal your funds. The most common scam is the \"phishing link\". Scammers will create fake Twitter accounts that look identical to a real project and post fake airdrop claim links.\n\nAlways verify the project's official Twitter handle and website URL. Never type your seed phrase into ANY website. Real airdrops only require a digital signature, not your recovery phrase.\n\nAnother golden rule: Use a burner wallet. Keep your main long-term holdings in a hardware wallet (like a Ledger), and only keep a small amount of funds for gas fees in your active airdrop farming wallet."
