      "excerpt": "Learn why blockchains charge fees for transactions and strategies to pay less gas.",
      "content": "A gas fee is the cost required to perform a transaction or execute a smart contract on a blockchain network. It compensates the miners or validators who process and secure the transactions.\n\nGas fees fluctuate based on network demand. When a highly anticipated NFT mints or a massive airdrop is claimable, the network gets congested, and gas prices spike.\n\nTo minimize your costs, try tracking network metrics using tools like an ETH Gas Tracker. Interact with protocols during weekends or early morning hours (US time) when global network activity is historically at its lowest."
